      "settings": {
        "title": "Our Accessories Buying Process",
        "copy": "MoMA was the first museum to establish a curatorial department dedicated to architecture and design. That legacy continues to inform how we source accessories today—products that combine beauty, function, and purpose. \nOur buying team takes a global, hands-on approach. We travel to shops, studios, and showrooms around the world to discover and assess products in person. We also dive into the stories behind each designer or brand to ensure their work aligns with our values.\nWhether searching for travel, jewelry and handbags, we focus on accessories that are: \n\n• Designed with longevity in mind—timeless, trend-aware, or nostalgic\n • Made with intention, often using sustainable or innovative materials\n • Beautifully crafted and practical for everyday life",
